# CODEOWNERS — vigil-sovereign
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT. A CODEOWNERS file has existed since the CRUCIBLE engine was
# vendored in, at `engine/crucible/.github/CODEOWNERS` — where GitHub never reads it. GitHub looks in
# exactly three places for the repository it belongs to: `.github/CODEOWNERS`, `CODEOWNERS`, or
# `docs/CODEOWNERS`, all relative to the ROOT of the repo. A file nested under a subdirectory is inert,
# so the ownership rule it states has never actually applied to a single pull request here.
#
# That mattered because the as-built documentation cited it as a protection. It was a claim about a
# file, not about the repository's behaviour.
#
# NOTE ON WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT ENFORCE. CODEOWNERS assigns REVIEWERS. It only BLOCKS a merge when
# branch protection also has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled — which it does not today (there
# is no required-reviews rule on `main` at all). So this file makes ownership explicit and requests the
# review; it does not by itself gate anything. Do not describe it as a gate until that setting is on.

